<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<model>
    <name>vacuum_dock</name>
    <version>1.0</version>
    <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>
    <author>
        <name>Ilia O.</name>
        <email>iliao@kaia.ai</email>
    </author>
    <description>Auto-empty and mop-wash charging dock for oomwoo_one, 0.460 x 0.340 x 0.580 m, authored from primitives: a flat-topped tower over a drive-in bay the robot reverses into, with plain faces and 0.030 m rounded vertical edges top and bottom. The bay is 0.400 wide (20 mm either side of the 0.359 m bumper), 0.210 deep and 0.170 high (73 mm over the 0.097 m turret). That depth is set by the LiDAR: the turret sits 0.0745 m forward of the robot centre, so backed fully in it ends up 0.254 m from the bay back face, 0.044 m clear of the mouth, with 58 percent of the robot inside. The bay floor is flush with the room floor, so there is nothing to climb, and the bay carries NO collision geometry (only the tower, back block and side walls do) so the robot can sit in it without the physics ejecting it. Brass charging contacts sit on the back face at bumper height.</description>
</model>
